dicating weakness, but they could easily have a low pair or a better high card (King or Queen). Betting as a bluff might work to fold out better high cards, but the pot is small (unraised limped pot), and risking chips on a pure bluff with zero equity is generally not worth the reward in this spot. Checking allows you to see the showdown for free; if the opponent has a total airball worse than yours, you win, otherwise, you lose the minimum.\n\nReason: You have only high card value with a mediocre kicker. The pot is small, and the opponent has shown passivity but could easily call a small bet with a bottom pair or high card. Checking minimizes loss and variance.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
